summary:
  An address StreamKind has learnt to be FLAC or Ogg still gets the writer that cuts segments.

history:
  MPEG-TS segments hold MP3 and AAC. Measured: FLAC and Vorbis written
  into them come out unplayable, with ffmpeg exiting 0. The writer looks at
  the bytes itself and would send such a stream to the single file, but a kind
  that is already known spares the look and the head file.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
      return known !== "flac" && known !== "ogg" && known !== "ogg-flac";

replace:
      return true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_only_an_address_that_may_be_mp3_or_aac_is_cut.
